   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/>N/A<br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><span>Strategic Partnerships Manager, Washington State Department of Commerce; Founder and Owner, Perez Consulting; Learning Network Equity Lead, Washington Communities for Children; Professional Development Instructor, Puyallup School District; Business Instructor and Coach, Pierce County Business Accelerator Program; Executive Leadership Coach, Workforce Central</span><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/><span>B.A. Law, Economics, &amp; Public Policy, University of Washington</span><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/><span>Executive Committee Member, Pierce County Community Engagement Task Force; Former President and Founder, Tacoma Women of Color Collective</span><br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p><span>As the daughter of immigrants and a mother to two young children,&nbsp; I see clearly the challenges we are facing. No family should have to choose between rent and putting food on the table. I&rsquo;m running to bring new leadership to the 29th LD that is focused on our shared values and ensuring everyone can thrive.&nbsp; In Olympia,&nbsp; I&rsquo;ll advocate for workers rights, fair taxation, reproductive freedom, and protecting immigrant communities.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p><span>Endorsed:</span><span> 29th LD Democrats; Washington State Labor Council; Tacoma Firefighters Local 31; City Councilmembers Bushnell, Diaz, Hines, Rumbaugh, Sadalge, Scott, and Walker; Parks Commissioner Lee, and Port Commissioner Ang.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<div><span><br />\r\n</span></div><br/><br/>",
