   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p><span>Washington State Representative, 29th Legislative District (four terms); Deputy Majority Floor Leader, Chair of the Black Members Caucus and Members of Color Caucus, and Co-Chair of the Social Equity in Cannabis Task Force. School Board Director, Franklin Pierce Schools.</span></p>\r\n<div><span><br />\r\n</span></div><br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><p>U.S. Army Veteran, Landlord/Tenant Coordinator, Mortgage Banker, Diversity Trainer, and Domestic Violence; Sexual Assault Advocate.</p>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<div>\r\n<p><span>Saint Martin&rsquo;s University, B.A. Psychology, 1995.</span></p>\r\n<div><span><br />\r\n</span></div>\r\n</div><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/><span></span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Commissioner, Pierce County Housing Authority; Board Member, Community Healthcare, Member, City of Tacoma, MLK Planning Committee; Volunteer, Homeless Feeding Program, Altheimer Memorial Church.</span>\r\n<div><span><br />\r\n</span></div>\r\n<p><span></span></p><br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p><span>For 34 years, I have called Pierce County home. I&rsquo;ve fought for working families, seniors, people with disabilities, healthcare, public safety, and economic opportunity. I have supported legislation and appropriations that benefit the 29th; capped rental increases, reformed zoning laws for affordable housing, supported small business, and made public safety investments.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p><span>I&rsquo;m unbought and unbossed. I believe leadership requires values, judgment, and independent thinking &mdash; not political pressure or ideology. I build coalitions and make thoughtful decisions guided by the people I represent. I will continue fighting for equity, public safety, healthcare, housing, and opportunities for everyone in our district.</span></p>\r\n<div><span><br />\r\n</span></div><br/><br/>",
